1
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:39,477
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:44,482 --> 00:00:47,610
There is a wide gap
between the train and the platform.

3
00:00:47,694 --> 00:00:50,238
Please watch your step.

4
00:00:51,531 --> 00:00:52,907
The doors are opening.

5
00:00:55,869 --> 00:00:58,204
Hey, we're here. We have to go.

6
00:00:58,288 --> 00:00:59,122
Get up.

7
00:01:02,917 --> 00:01:04,627
Man, I'm tired.

8
00:01:06,629 --> 00:01:08,298
We almost missed our stop.

9
00:01:12,886 --> 00:01:14,888
I had fun today. See you tomorrow.

10
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,598
Okay.

11
00:01:32,405 --> 00:01:33,531
Go already.

12
00:01:50,131 --> 00:01:52,717
You two are amazing.

13
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,845
How did you pull off
such great chemistry so quickly?

14
00:01:56,346 --> 00:01:57,764
Nicely done.

15
00:01:57,847 --> 00:01:59,682
I knew you two could do it.

16
00:01:59,766 --> 00:02:01,434
With skills like this,

17
00:02:01,517 --> 00:02:03,269
you'll shut everyone up for good.

18
00:02:03,811 --> 00:02:06,731
You two are ready
for the progress recital now, right?

19
00:02:06,814 --> 00:02:08,191
-Mr. Do.
-Mr. Do.

20
00:02:09,359 --> 00:02:11,527
If we have to perform anyway,

21
00:02:12,153 --> 00:02:14,113
how about we audition
for the Noblesse Classical Concert?

22
00:02:14,697 --> 00:02:16,074
Noblesse Classical Concert?

23
00:02:16,157 --> 00:02:18,368
The one sponsored
by the Seodam Foundation?

24
00:02:19,035 --> 00:02:19,953
Yes.

25
00:02:21,996 --> 00:02:26,167
I don't know. Even established performers
have trouble getting a spot there.

26
00:02:26,668 --> 00:02:28,628
Let's do the progress recital first and--

27
00:02:28,711 --> 00:02:29,629
No, sir.

28
00:02:29,712 --> 00:02:32,799
I'd rather play at the Noblesse Classical
than at the progress recital.

29
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:36,803
I hope you'll respect
my opinion this time.

30
00:02:40,265 --> 00:02:41,349
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

31
00:02:41,432 --> 00:02:43,184
Bye. Take care.

32
00:02:49,857 --> 00:02:50,692
Hey.

33
00:02:52,485 --> 00:02:53,611
Why did you tell him

34
00:02:53,695 --> 00:02:56,364
you wanted to try out for that concert
without talking to me first?

35
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,574
Oh, sorry.

36
00:02:59,951 --> 00:03:01,619
I'm sorry for not asking first,

37
00:03:02,537 --> 00:03:04,122
but will you go with me on this?

38
00:03:05,081 --> 00:03:07,292
The Noblesse Classical Concert
was my goal from the very beginning.

39
00:03:10,044 --> 00:03:11,337
What exactly is it?

40
00:03:11,421 --> 00:03:13,715
Why does it have to be that concert?

41
00:03:14,882 --> 00:03:16,676
Even for the Noblesse Classical Concert?

42
00:03:17,844 --> 00:03:20,847
Fine. Let's see you try.

43
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:23,975
But if I still feel the same way then…

44
00:03:25,893 --> 00:03:28,354
you'll need to take responsibility
for what you said.

45
00:03:31,065 --> 00:03:32,942
I can't go into detail right now.

46
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:34,986
But Jeong-yo,

47
00:03:36,029 --> 00:03:37,697
it's an important opportunity for me,

48
00:03:38,781 --> 00:03:39,866
so I need your help.

49
00:03:42,702 --> 00:03:44,245
You can do that, right?

50
00:03:47,749 --> 00:03:52,503
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

51
00:03:53,338 --> 00:03:55,340
EPISODE 3

52
00:04:03,848 --> 00:04:05,975
It sounds a little stiff here.

53
00:04:06,059 --> 00:04:08,478
Don't worry about the tempo,
and let it flow naturally.

54
00:04:08,561 --> 00:04:12,190
But if I let it flow too much,
wouldn't it lose that Bach feel?

55
00:04:12,273 --> 00:04:13,900
Everyone knows how it should sound.

56
00:04:13,983 --> 00:04:16,986
Instead of playing the conventional way…

57
00:04:25,661 --> 00:04:26,913
Hey, guys!

58
00:04:28,706 --> 00:04:30,375
-Look who's here with snacks!
-Nice!

59
00:04:33,127 --> 00:04:36,297
Hey, that's not how you eat this.
This is how you do it.

60
00:04:37,673 --> 00:04:38,841
-It's good, right?
-Yeah.

61
00:04:41,427 --> 00:04:42,720
-Hurry up and eat.
-Hold on.

62
00:04:44,389 --> 00:04:46,432
Now one for you, Pi-o.

63
00:04:46,516 --> 00:04:49,185
All right. One, two, three!

64
00:05:13,126 --> 00:05:13,960
Any word?

65
00:05:21,884 --> 00:05:23,594
NOBLESSE CLASSICAL CONCERT
AUDITION RESULT: PASSED

66
00:05:26,639 --> 00:05:27,890
Yes!

67
00:06:02,508 --> 00:06:04,844
SCHEDULED GUEST SOLOIST KIM NA-RAE

68
00:06:16,898 --> 00:06:17,815
Grandfather.

69
00:06:19,609 --> 00:06:20,443
I…

70
00:06:21,486 --> 00:06:24,739
passed the audition
for the Noblesse Classical Concert.

71
00:06:31,871 --> 00:06:35,082
Grandfather, I said I passed the audition.

72
00:06:36,417 --> 00:06:37,585
You'll come and watch, right?

73
00:06:40,338 --> 00:06:41,672
Grandfather, don't you remember?

74
00:06:41,756 --> 00:06:44,133
You said you'd watch me perform
if I got to play there--

75
00:06:44,217 --> 00:06:45,968
I said leave! Can't you see I'm busy?

76
00:06:50,890 --> 00:06:52,225
I'll decide whether I go or not.

77
00:07:19,335 --> 00:07:21,128
This is so tight and uncomfortable.

78
00:07:21,796 --> 00:07:24,048
I don't know
if I can play properly like this.

79
00:07:24,966 --> 00:07:28,135
I don't get it.
Why do all classical musicians wear this?

80
00:07:28,219 --> 00:07:30,012
Isn't this an outdated formality?

81
00:07:30,555 --> 00:07:33,140
Hey, take a look at this.
It feels so tight.

82
00:07:33,224 --> 00:07:34,475
Is my bow tie on right?

83
00:07:34,559 --> 00:07:35,726
Look.

84
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:37,186
Cut it out.

85
00:07:38,688 --> 00:07:40,398
What's with the cold shoulder?

86
00:07:44,569 --> 00:07:45,695
Are you nervous?

87
00:07:46,571 --> 00:07:48,698
I'm not nervous, so why are you?

88
00:07:48,781 --> 00:07:50,449
You've performed over a hundred times.

89
00:07:52,868 --> 00:07:56,038
Wow, you two look amazing.

90
00:07:56,122 --> 00:07:58,416
All right. Shall we go?

91
00:08:03,588 --> 00:08:04,547
What's his problem?

92
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,842
SEODAM ART CENTER

93
00:08:07,925 --> 00:08:09,552
AN EVENING OF YOUNG VIRTUOSOS

94
00:08:13,389 --> 00:08:15,975
-Hello.
-Please place it over here.

95
00:08:17,685 --> 00:08:19,020
Let's move this over a bit.

96
00:08:43,169 --> 00:08:44,962
There's a medical emergency.

97
00:09:06,484 --> 00:09:08,944
KANG PI-O, CHOI JEONG-YO (PIANO DUET)
J.S. BACH, CANTATA BWV 147, NO. 10

98
00:09:10,321 --> 00:09:11,447
Choi Jeong-yo.

99
00:09:14,950 --> 00:09:15,993
Choi Jeong-yo?

100
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,681
Hyun-soo.

101
00:09:37,765 --> 00:09:39,100
Hello, Seon-ju.

102
00:09:40,518 --> 00:09:42,395
You did a great job.

103
00:09:42,478 --> 00:09:44,271
You got those kids here in a month.

104
00:09:48,401 --> 00:09:49,985
It'll be a good performance, right?

105
00:09:51,696 --> 00:09:54,490
We need to show them
what they're up against.

106
00:09:54,573 --> 00:09:55,658
You're confident, right?

107
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:01,789
-Oh.
-I'll see you afterward.

108
00:10:01,872 --> 00:10:03,416
-Okay, see you later.
-All right.

109
00:10:07,461 --> 00:10:08,504
Hyun-soo.

110
00:10:13,384 --> 00:10:15,386
Hey, you made it.

111
00:10:16,053 --> 00:10:18,389
Pi-o really wanted to perform here.

112
00:10:19,890 --> 00:10:21,475
It's all thanks to you.

113
00:10:22,059 --> 00:10:25,062
No, Pi-o made this happen on his own.

114
00:10:25,146 --> 00:10:26,564
I didn't do anything.

115
00:10:28,649 --> 00:10:31,944
By the way, it says Pi-o's partner is

116
00:10:32,027 --> 00:10:33,404
-Choi--
-Mr. Do?

117
00:10:33,487 --> 00:10:35,322
Sorry, I'll see you later.

118
00:10:35,406 --> 00:10:36,282
Yes?

119
00:10:38,325 --> 00:10:39,368
Please take your seats.

120
00:10:48,419 --> 00:10:49,503
I can't wait!

121
00:10:50,004 --> 00:10:51,046
Settle down.

122
00:11:10,441 --> 00:11:15,780
Thank you for joining us today
at the Noblesse Classical Concert.

123
00:11:15,863 --> 00:11:18,407
For years, the Noblesse Classical Concert

124
00:11:18,491 --> 00:11:21,076
has earned a stellar reputation
as a launching pad

125
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:24,038
-for discovering and showcasing artists
-I'm okay.

126
00:11:24,121 --> 00:11:26,540
who have put Korea on the world stage.

127
00:11:27,666 --> 00:11:30,836
Let's welcome to the stage
the rising stars of classical music,

128
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:35,132
starting with our first performers
of the evening.

129
00:11:35,216 --> 00:11:36,217
Everyone,

130
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,928
please welcome them
with a big round of applause.

131
00:12:13,963 --> 00:12:15,756
There's a medical emergency.

132
00:12:18,551 --> 00:12:19,385
Mom!

133
00:12:20,261 --> 00:12:22,721
-Mom!
-What's going on? Are you okay?

134
00:12:22,805 --> 00:12:25,724
-Excuse me, wake up!
-Mom! You're okay, right?

135
00:12:25,808 --> 00:12:26,809
Mom!

136
00:12:30,938 --> 00:12:31,772
What's happening?

137
00:12:46,954 --> 00:12:49,623
He's having trouble breathing.
What's going on?

138
00:12:53,919 --> 00:12:55,129
What's wrong?

139
00:12:57,464 --> 00:12:59,341
What's gotten into you?

140
00:12:59,842 --> 00:13:01,302
Get it together!

141
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:04,597
What are you doing here?

142
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,348
The audience is waiting.

143
00:13:08,017 --> 00:13:10,561
You two will not perform today.

144
00:13:11,604 --> 00:13:13,689
Go bring the quartet right now.

145
00:13:13,772 --> 00:13:15,065
-Yes, sir.
-Hurry.

146
00:13:15,149 --> 00:13:16,275
Wait…

147
00:13:29,914 --> 00:13:30,748
Mom.

148
00:13:32,082 --> 00:13:33,083
Mom.

149
00:13:33,792 --> 00:13:34,835
Mom…

150
00:13:37,046 --> 00:13:38,213
Mom…

151
00:13:46,221 --> 00:13:47,097
Jeong-yo.

152
00:13:48,849 --> 00:13:50,059
Choi Jeong-yo.

153
00:13:50,976 --> 00:13:52,144
Don't think about anything.

154
00:13:53,812 --> 00:13:55,064
Just focus on my voice

155
00:13:56,231 --> 00:13:58,025
and my playing.

156
00:13:59,985 --> 00:14:01,904
I can't. I can't do it.

157
00:14:04,573 --> 00:14:05,783
Do you trust me or not?

158
00:14:07,743 --> 00:14:08,744
Because I trust you.

159
00:14:10,162 --> 00:14:11,705
We practiced this hundreds of times.

160
00:14:12,414 --> 00:14:14,625
What's different now? Absolutely nothing.

161
00:14:14,708 --> 00:14:17,002
Ignore everyone else.

162
00:14:17,086 --> 00:14:19,088
Forget where we are.

163
00:14:20,005 --> 00:14:21,590
Just focus on my playing.

164
00:14:23,092 --> 00:14:24,635
Just like you did in the practice room.

165
00:15:30,743 --> 00:15:31,577
Play freely…

166
00:15:34,121 --> 00:15:35,039
like that day.

167
00:16:50,072 --> 00:16:51,073
It's the boy

168
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:53,200
from the Donghan Junior Piano Competition.

169
00:16:54,451 --> 00:16:55,410
Choi Jeong-yo.

170
00:19:26,895 --> 00:19:28,939
I'm totally blown away.

171
00:19:29,022 --> 00:19:30,816
I had no idea he was so amazing.

172
00:19:30,899 --> 00:19:32,025
How does he play so well?

173
00:19:32,109 --> 00:19:34,736
He was blindfolded
but didn't miss a single note.

174
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:36,321
It was insanely cool, wasn't it?

175
00:19:36,405 --> 00:19:37,447
I told you guys.

176
00:19:37,531 --> 00:19:40,325
He's in a totally different league.

177
00:19:40,826 --> 00:19:41,994
-You were so right.
-Totally.

178
00:19:42,077 --> 00:19:43,078
Let's go, son.

179
00:19:43,954 --> 00:19:45,914
Excuse me, ladies?

180
00:19:49,710 --> 00:19:50,711
Hello.

181
00:19:51,253 --> 00:19:54,006
So did you enjoy the concert?

182
00:19:54,089 --> 00:19:55,215
Yes, well…

183
00:19:56,341 --> 00:19:57,884
I suppose we did.

184
00:20:00,595 --> 00:20:04,933
Did it help clear up
any misunderstandings you had about me?

185
00:20:25,996 --> 00:20:27,331
Oh, okay.

186
00:20:27,414 --> 00:20:30,167
It's great we made it through, right?

187
00:20:31,126 --> 00:20:32,294
Dude!

188
00:20:32,377 --> 00:20:34,796
Hey, cut it out. I can't breathe!

189
00:20:36,298 --> 00:20:38,175
Choi Jeong-yo! Kang Pi-o!

190
00:20:40,302 --> 00:20:42,512
Great job, you two.

191
00:20:42,596 --> 00:20:43,972
I really mean it.

192
00:20:44,056 --> 00:20:46,224
Thank you for doing so well.

193
00:20:46,308 --> 00:20:49,061
But what happened in the beginning?

194
00:20:49,644 --> 00:20:51,730
Jeong-yo was a little nervous,

195
00:20:51,813 --> 00:20:54,107
so I suggested the blindfold.

196
00:20:54,191 --> 00:20:56,526
Wow, Pi-o. I'm so proud of you.

197
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:58,445
How'd you come up with that idea?

198
00:21:00,072 --> 00:21:00,947
Yes?

199
00:21:06,328 --> 00:21:07,496
Hello, sir.

200
00:21:09,456 --> 00:21:10,957
Did you enjoy the performance?

201
00:21:11,541 --> 00:21:12,959
There was a bit of trouble at first.

202
00:21:13,043 --> 00:21:13,960
You must've been startled.

203
00:21:14,669 --> 00:21:15,629
What happened?

204
00:21:16,254 --> 00:21:20,050
It looks like Jeong-yo
suddenly got a little nervous.

205
00:21:20,133 --> 00:21:22,386
Luckily, Pi-o handled the situation well,

206
00:21:22,469 --> 00:21:24,262
so they pulled through just fine.

207
00:21:25,389 --> 00:21:26,390
I see.

208
00:21:26,473 --> 00:21:28,266
Today wasn't half bad.

209
00:21:29,810 --> 00:21:32,229
Invite me to your next performance.

210
00:21:34,606 --> 00:21:36,316
See you later. I loved the performance.

211
00:21:44,866 --> 00:21:47,077
What was that kid's name again?

212
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,412
Who do you mean?

213
00:21:48,495 --> 00:21:49,704
The one next to Pi-o.

214
00:21:49,788 --> 00:21:52,249
Oh, it's Jeong-yo. Choi Jeong-yo.

215
00:21:52,833 --> 00:21:55,043
I recruited him myself. Good call, right?

216
00:21:56,002 --> 00:21:57,421
I want to see him play again,

217
00:21:57,504 --> 00:21:59,881
so bring him
to the orchestra rehearsal room.

218
00:21:59,965 --> 00:22:00,799
-I will.
-Hey.

219
00:22:00,882 --> 00:22:03,677
If you knew someone that talented,
you should've told me first.

220
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:06,555
I didn't know he was that good.

221
00:22:07,722 --> 00:22:09,182
-Seriously.
-Goodness.

222
00:22:11,435 --> 00:22:12,894
Hello, ma'am.

223
00:22:15,021 --> 00:22:16,106
Hey, aren't we celebrating?

224
00:22:19,985 --> 00:22:20,819
I should get going.

225
00:22:21,778 --> 00:22:23,613
Okay, take care.

226
00:22:23,697 --> 00:22:25,073
I really enjoyed the performance.

227
00:22:25,157 --> 00:22:26,116
Thank you.

228
00:22:28,869 --> 00:22:29,953
Are you calling it a night?

229
00:22:30,537 --> 00:22:32,164
After such a good performance?

230
00:22:34,583 --> 00:22:35,417
I'll message you.

231
00:22:37,085 --> 00:22:37,919
Okay.

232
00:22:43,592 --> 00:22:45,719
I really enjoyed the performance.

233
00:22:45,802 --> 00:22:48,847
Goodness, you've got amazing skills.

234
00:22:49,347 --> 00:22:50,182
Thank you.

235
00:22:51,266 --> 00:22:52,726
Say hi. This is my mom.

236
00:22:53,685 --> 00:22:54,895
Remember how I told you

237
00:22:54,978 --> 00:22:57,564
that she's the head
of a classical music agency?

238
00:22:59,483 --> 00:23:00,358
Hello.

239
00:23:01,818 --> 00:23:04,446
You haven't signed with
an agency yet, right?

240
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:26,218
What's wrong?

241
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:33,391
What aren't you happy about? Just tell me.

242
00:23:34,351 --> 00:23:35,310
What was that?

243
00:23:36,311 --> 00:23:37,479
Why didn't you tell me?

244
00:23:37,562 --> 00:23:39,022
-About what?
-Choi Jeong-yo!

245
00:23:40,565 --> 00:23:42,734
He's the same kid
who crushed you seven years ago!

246
00:23:42,817 --> 00:23:44,528
So? What about it?

247
00:23:45,070 --> 00:23:48,114
I played better than ever today,

248
00:23:48,198 --> 00:23:51,409
and even Grandfather said
he wanted to see my next performance.

249
00:23:51,993 --> 00:23:52,953
Your performance?

250
00:23:53,620 --> 00:23:56,206
Sure, you played better than usual.

251
00:23:56,289 --> 00:23:57,123
But you know what?

252
00:23:57,624 --> 00:24:00,710
Thanks to you,
that kid pulled off a performance

253
00:24:00,794 --> 00:24:02,087
that should've been a disaster.

254
00:24:02,170 --> 00:24:03,380
You basically saved

255
00:24:04,130 --> 00:24:05,507
your biggest competition.

256
00:24:06,675 --> 00:24:07,801
Mom.

257
00:24:08,468 --> 00:24:11,346
Didn't you see
how well I performed on stage?

258
00:24:12,180 --> 00:24:15,225
For the first time in my life,
I enjoyed being on stage

259
00:24:15,308 --> 00:24:17,269
and got the best reaction
from the audience.

260
00:24:17,352 --> 00:24:19,396
You think that's because you did well?

261
00:24:19,479 --> 00:24:21,356
Choi Jeong-yo was the star today!

262
00:24:22,399 --> 00:24:24,025
The audience didn't care about you.

263
00:24:24,818 --> 00:24:26,653
You think I'm overreacting,
but just watch.

264
00:24:26,736 --> 00:24:29,906
Social media will be flooded
with Choi Jeong-yo's name tonight.

265
00:24:29,990 --> 00:24:33,535
And you'll sit there like a fool
and let him take first place again!

266
00:24:35,495 --> 00:24:36,621
This won't do.

267
00:24:38,331 --> 00:24:40,792
Start preparing for competitions today.

268
00:24:49,301 --> 00:24:52,095
#ONCE IN A GENERATION TALENT
#BLINDFOLDED PIANIST #CHOI JEONG-YO

269
00:25:01,938 --> 00:25:03,189
Pi-o.

270
00:25:03,273 --> 00:25:05,942
I knew you could do it.
Today's performance was the best!

271
00:25:06,026 --> 00:25:08,153
I only had eyes for you.

272
00:26:01,623 --> 00:26:03,041
Are we really not celebrating?

273
00:26:03,875 --> 00:26:04,876
Can't you come out?

274
00:26:10,131 --> 00:26:10,965
CALLING KANG PI-O

275
00:26:26,773 --> 00:26:27,899
MS. YOON

276
00:26:27,982 --> 00:26:29,776
Great job today.

277
00:26:29,859 --> 00:26:32,028
I need you to come somewhere
with me tomorrow.

278
00:27:05,395 --> 00:27:07,522
CHOI JEONG-YO:
ARE WE REALLY NOT CELEBRATING?

279
00:27:13,570 --> 00:27:15,488
How do you usually practice?

280
00:27:15,572 --> 00:27:17,031
Do you have a special routine?

281
00:27:17,115 --> 00:27:17,949
What?

282
00:27:18,032 --> 00:27:20,577
Sorry, I just play however I want.

283
00:27:21,494 --> 00:27:23,121
You play however you want?

284
00:27:23,204 --> 00:27:25,373
Wait, so you're actually a natural?

285
00:27:25,457 --> 00:27:28,960
He's got to be a natural
to play with a rhythm like that.

286
00:27:29,043 --> 00:27:31,087
What's your favorite piece to play?

287
00:27:31,796 --> 00:27:33,757
Rachmaninoff? Liszt?

288
00:27:33,840 --> 00:27:36,885
I bet you play Barber or Kapustin well
with your sense of rhythm.

289
00:27:36,968 --> 00:27:37,802
Am I right?

290
00:27:37,886 --> 00:27:40,597
But can't you see him
playing Schubert too?

291
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:41,765
Yeah, totally.

292
00:27:41,848 --> 00:27:44,934
The way he carries out the phrases
sounds so smooth and deliberate.

293
00:27:45,518 --> 00:27:47,937
But he doesn't rush the tempo either.

294
00:27:48,021 --> 00:27:50,148
He'd be good at playing slow pieces too.

295
00:27:50,231 --> 00:27:51,858
You were amazing.

296
00:27:51,941 --> 00:27:55,528
-Can I watch you practice?
-Sorry. Let's talk later.

297
00:27:55,612 --> 00:27:57,781
Sorry. I'm really sorry.

298
00:27:58,782 --> 00:28:00,450
-It's your fault.
-What did I do?

299
00:28:00,533 --> 00:28:01,451
Hey, Pi-o.

300
00:28:02,911 --> 00:28:04,579
-Did you see my message?
-Yeah.

301
00:28:04,662 --> 00:28:07,665
Then why didn't you reply?

302
00:28:08,208 --> 00:28:09,918
That's so mean. I waited all night.

303
00:28:12,128 --> 00:28:14,506
Anyway, let's celebrate sometime.

304
00:28:15,173 --> 00:28:17,675
Thanks to you,
we got through the performance.

305
00:28:18,927 --> 00:28:20,428
There's no need for that.

306
00:28:21,346 --> 00:28:23,097
I didn't do it just for you.

307
00:28:24,098 --> 00:28:25,058
Come on.

308
00:28:25,642 --> 00:28:28,102
But I don't feel comfortable
not thanking you.

309
00:28:30,438 --> 00:28:33,274
By the way, I've been thinking.

310
00:28:33,358 --> 00:28:37,195
Let's keep going and play more duets.

311
00:28:37,862 --> 00:28:41,825
There are some four-hand pieces
I've really been wanting to play.

312
00:28:41,908 --> 00:28:44,327
Oh, and I worked on this yesterday…

313
00:28:44,410 --> 00:28:45,787
We're done, Jeong-yo.

314
00:28:46,788 --> 00:28:48,706
I'll be too busy
preparing for competitions.

315
00:28:49,374 --> 00:28:51,251
If you want to play, find another partner.

316
00:28:52,794 --> 00:28:53,628
Hey.

317
00:28:55,004 --> 00:28:56,381
That's a bit harsh.

318
00:28:57,048 --> 00:28:59,843
I want to do it because it's you,
not just anyone.

319
00:29:00,426 --> 00:29:01,761
I get what you mean,

320
00:29:02,762 --> 00:29:04,347
but I don't have that kind of time.

321
00:29:05,557 --> 00:29:06,766
Find another partner.

322
00:29:19,153 --> 00:29:21,447
Hey, Ji-hye. Why are you calling so early?

323
00:29:21,531 --> 00:29:22,574
By any chance,

324
00:29:22,657 --> 00:29:26,077
were you thinking about
signing Choi Jeong-yo?

325
00:29:27,537 --> 00:29:29,622
Where is this coming from?

326
00:29:29,706 --> 00:29:31,082
If you were, drop the idea.

327
00:29:31,165 --> 00:29:33,334
But if you insist on signing him,

328
00:29:34,210 --> 00:29:36,254
Pi-o will no longer be
part of your agency.

329
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:40,091
And I want to know where Hyun-soo lives.

330
00:29:41,009 --> 00:29:42,302
Oh, well--

331
00:29:42,385 --> 00:29:44,304
I can't take notes right now,

332
00:29:45,096 --> 00:29:46,848
so text me his address.

333
00:29:55,273 --> 00:29:57,442
How did you know where I live?

334
00:29:57,525 --> 00:29:58,735
Can I come in?

335
00:30:16,419 --> 00:30:18,504
-I'll get you some coffee.
-Pi-o.

336
00:30:19,589 --> 00:30:21,174
Why did you pair him with that kid?

337
00:30:22,634 --> 00:30:23,468
What?

338
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:28,598
You did that on purpose
to make that kid stand out.

339
00:30:28,681 --> 00:30:30,892
What on earth are you talking about?

340
00:30:30,975 --> 00:30:32,560
You did it because you hate me.

341
00:30:33,144 --> 00:30:34,145
Because

342
00:30:34,729 --> 00:30:36,064
I betrayed you.

343
00:30:38,316 --> 00:30:39,484
Fine.

344
00:30:40,944 --> 00:30:44,697
It's true that I have
hard feelings toward you.

345
00:30:46,157 --> 00:30:47,367
But that doesn't mean

346
00:30:48,117 --> 00:30:49,619
I'd do something like that

347
00:30:50,703 --> 00:30:52,497
because of the past.

348
00:30:55,208 --> 00:30:58,378
I felt guilty about asking you
to take Pi-o under your wing.

349
00:30:59,837 --> 00:31:02,006
But I still asked.

350
00:31:03,132 --> 00:31:04,509
Because…

351
00:31:05,176 --> 00:31:06,135
Because…

352
00:31:07,261 --> 00:31:08,763
I'm Pi-o's mother.

353
00:31:10,139 --> 00:31:11,599
I felt bad about it,

354
00:31:12,308 --> 00:31:13,393
but I had to…

355
00:31:15,019 --> 00:31:16,854
save my son.

356
00:31:32,412 --> 00:31:33,830
You have no idea.

357
00:31:34,455 --> 00:31:35,456
You don't know…

358
00:31:37,375 --> 00:31:39,585
what Pi-o and I have been through.

359
00:31:40,795 --> 00:31:43,548
You saw the way my father treated us.

360
00:31:45,508 --> 00:31:46,801
I understand

361
00:31:47,885 --> 00:31:49,303
how tough things were for you.

362
00:31:50,304 --> 00:31:51,806
But don't get the wrong idea.

363
00:31:53,141 --> 00:31:57,103
I truly thought pairing them up
would bring out the best in each other.

364
00:31:57,186 --> 00:31:59,063
And yesterday's performance…

365
00:32:01,065 --> 00:32:03,484
clearly brought out Pi-o's true potential.

366
00:32:05,111 --> 00:32:06,070
It's your anxiety.

367
00:32:07,864 --> 00:32:10,116
It's playing tricks on your imagination.

368
00:32:10,199 --> 00:32:11,325
Ji-hye,

369
00:32:12,076 --> 00:32:15,747
Pi-o is a lot more resilient
than you think.

370
00:32:16,581 --> 00:32:17,498
Then,

371
00:32:19,167 --> 00:32:20,418
can you help Pi-o…

372
00:32:22,170 --> 00:32:24,797
place in a competition?

373
00:32:27,050 --> 00:32:28,676
You know better than anyone

374
00:32:29,177 --> 00:32:30,803
that the only way to survive this industry

375
00:32:30,887 --> 00:32:33,514
is to place
in an international competition.

376
00:32:35,016 --> 00:32:36,434
Hyun-soo.

377
00:32:37,310 --> 00:32:39,270
Help him place in a competition.

378
00:32:41,064 --> 00:32:41,898
Please?

379
00:33:09,759 --> 00:33:10,843
Hello.

380
00:33:13,179 --> 00:33:14,013
Hi.

381
00:33:15,723 --> 00:33:18,559
I enjoyed the performance yesterday.

382
00:33:20,228 --> 00:33:21,187
Thank you.

383
00:33:21,854 --> 00:33:25,108
But I'm quite worried right now.

384
00:33:26,317 --> 00:33:29,904
Pi-o doesn't have time to waste
playing four hands right now.

385
00:33:31,781 --> 00:33:33,199
Are you here to pick up Pi-o?

386
00:33:36,285 --> 00:33:37,245
Get in, Jeong-yo.

387
00:33:37,328 --> 00:33:39,122
Oh, okay.

388
00:33:40,289 --> 00:33:41,124
Goodbye.

389
00:33:44,752 --> 00:33:46,212
Where are you going?

390
00:33:46,712 --> 00:33:49,382
After watching yesterday's concert,

391
00:33:49,465 --> 00:33:51,092
Mr. Kang wanted to see Jeong-yo.

392
00:33:54,971 --> 00:33:56,055
See you at home.

393
00:34:03,396 --> 00:34:04,230
Mom.

394
00:34:05,815 --> 00:34:06,691
Mom?

395
00:34:09,944 --> 00:34:11,362
Have you heard or not?

396
00:34:11,445 --> 00:34:12,697
About what?

397
00:34:12,780 --> 00:34:15,324
Didn't your grandfather tell you

398
00:34:16,200 --> 00:34:17,785
he asked to see Choi Jeong-yo?

399
00:34:27,753 --> 00:34:30,173
Now do you understand what I'm saying?

400
00:34:31,215 --> 00:34:32,884
I knew something was up last night.

401
00:34:33,801 --> 00:34:36,762
This is why you need to
crush the competition from the start!

402
00:34:37,263 --> 00:34:40,892
I asked Hyun-soo to help you prepare
for an international competition.

403
00:34:40,975 --> 00:34:42,226
Just focus on that.

404
00:34:42,310 --> 00:34:45,021
Snap out of it and pull yourself together!

405
00:34:47,773 --> 00:34:49,609
PRINCIPAL CONDUCTOR'S OFFICE

406
00:34:53,321 --> 00:34:54,906
-Mr. Kang?
-Come in.

407
00:34:55,406 --> 00:34:56,324
Let's go inside.

408
00:34:56,407 --> 00:34:57,241
Okay.

409
00:35:00,453 --> 00:35:01,370
Hello.

410
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:04,081
Say hello.

411
00:35:04,165 --> 00:35:06,125
This is Maestro Kang Seung-woon.

412
00:35:06,209 --> 00:35:07,960
He was Mr. Do's teacher.

413
00:35:10,671 --> 00:35:11,505
Hello.

414
00:35:13,299 --> 00:35:14,967
As I said before,

415
00:35:15,051 --> 00:35:17,720
he'll give you plenty of guidance,
so don't be intimidated.

416
00:35:17,803 --> 00:35:19,722
Don't be intimidated?

417
00:35:20,514 --> 00:35:22,934
I called you here
because I wanted to check something.

418
00:36:03,516 --> 00:36:04,558
Stop.

419
00:36:07,979 --> 00:36:09,981
You don't follow the sheet music.

420
00:36:11,399 --> 00:36:12,233
No, sir.

421
00:36:12,316 --> 00:36:16,112
Why play the left hand as a block chord
in measure eight instead of rolling it?

422
00:36:16,737 --> 00:36:18,739
Because that makes it sound more lively.

423
00:36:20,408 --> 00:36:22,576
You know what appassionato means, right?

424
00:36:24,036 --> 00:36:25,538
"Passionately," sir.

425
00:36:25,621 --> 00:36:28,249
Then why did you play
measure 33 with rubato?

426
00:36:28,332 --> 00:36:29,583
RUBATO: PLAYING WITH CHANGES TO SPEED

427
00:36:29,667 --> 00:36:31,168
Allowing some breathing room

428
00:36:32,003 --> 00:36:34,505
actually makes it feel like
a warm breeze is blowing through.

429
00:36:36,173 --> 00:36:38,718
I think Chopin would say it's fine.

430
00:36:39,302 --> 00:36:41,887
Chopin's intentions
are written in the score.

431
00:36:42,805 --> 00:36:44,265
Are you ignoring the score?

432
00:36:45,266 --> 00:36:47,351
The score is just music written down.

433
00:36:47,435 --> 00:36:49,729
I only wanted to hear the music itself.

434
00:36:52,356 --> 00:36:54,608
What goes through your mind
when you play the piano?

435
00:37:00,114 --> 00:37:01,198
Nothing.

436
00:37:02,700 --> 00:37:04,368
I actually try to clear my mind.

437
00:37:10,916 --> 00:37:12,960
Have you ever practiced a piano concerto?

438
00:37:14,879 --> 00:37:15,838
No, sir.

439
00:37:16,672 --> 00:37:17,631
All right then.

440
00:37:21,719 --> 00:37:23,387
There's an upcoming symphony festival.

441
00:37:24,347 --> 00:37:26,057
Audition for the concerto.

442
00:37:39,612 --> 00:37:40,821
Congratulations, Jeong-yo.

443
00:37:41,697 --> 00:37:44,492
It's amazing that he made you
such an offer right away.

444
00:37:45,743 --> 00:37:48,704
Trust me, this is truly remarkable.

445
00:37:48,788 --> 00:37:51,248
You have no idea, do you?

446
00:37:51,791 --> 00:37:52,625
No.

447
00:37:53,167 --> 00:37:57,129
Wow, I never expected you
to make such an impression this quickly.

448
00:37:57,838 --> 00:38:00,883
Pi-o might be disappointed
if you land the concerto,

449
00:38:00,966 --> 00:38:02,551
but that can't be helped.

450
00:38:08,557 --> 00:38:11,185
After all, I'm the one who recruited you.

451
00:38:13,020 --> 00:38:14,188
-Right.
-You know what?

452
00:38:15,231 --> 00:38:16,357
Close relationship or not,

453
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:18,984
I have to keep
my work and personal life separate.

454
00:38:20,236 --> 00:38:21,654
I'm sorry, but…

455
00:38:21,737 --> 00:38:22,613
Yes?

456
00:38:23,531 --> 00:38:25,282
What exactly is

457
00:38:26,409 --> 00:38:28,202
your relationship to Pi-o?

458
00:38:29,328 --> 00:38:30,162
Goodness.

459
00:38:34,083 --> 00:38:35,126
You didn't know?

460
00:38:36,168 --> 00:38:38,587
Pi-o is my grandson.

461
00:38:39,255 --> 00:38:40,214
Legally, that is.

462
00:38:41,507 --> 00:38:43,843
But Mr. Kang is his real grandfather.

463
00:38:46,178 --> 00:38:47,471
Mr. Kang and I are married,

464
00:38:47,555 --> 00:38:49,807
and he has a family
from his first marriage.

465
00:38:50,433 --> 00:38:53,060
That's how Pi-o became my grandson.

466
00:38:53,144 --> 00:38:55,563
The adult world
is a bit complicated, isn't it?

467
00:38:57,064 --> 00:38:59,108
Anyway, all you have to do is work hard.

468
00:38:59,191 --> 00:39:01,610
I'll take care of everything else.

469
00:39:02,945 --> 00:39:03,904
Jeong-yo.

470
00:39:06,407 --> 00:39:08,784
To tell you the truth,

471
00:39:09,493 --> 00:39:13,456
Mr. Kang has spent years looking for
genuine, raw talent to perform with.

472
00:39:15,666 --> 00:39:16,500
I…

473
00:39:18,252 --> 00:39:20,129
-Ms. Yoon.
-Yes?

474
00:39:22,548 --> 00:39:23,674
I'd rather not…

475
00:39:26,010 --> 00:39:27,219
audition for the concerto.

476
00:39:30,222 --> 00:39:31,056
What?

477
00:39:49,533 --> 00:39:53,787
WE NEED TO TALK. LET'S MEET UP.

478
00:40:00,377 --> 00:40:01,712
We need to talk.

479
00:40:01,795 --> 00:40:03,255
Let's meet up.

480
00:40:03,339 --> 00:40:04,173
UNREAD

481
00:40:05,299 --> 00:40:06,217
Seriously?

482
00:40:07,301 --> 00:40:08,427
CALLING KANG PI-O

483
00:40:30,658 --> 00:40:31,492
Kang Pi-o.

484
00:40:34,245 --> 00:40:35,913
What are you doing here?

485
00:40:36,497 --> 00:40:38,707
Why won't you answer my calls or texts?

486
00:40:39,583 --> 00:40:40,918
Was I supposed to?

487
00:40:41,502 --> 00:40:42,461
We need to talk.

488
00:40:43,671 --> 00:40:44,922
I have nothing to say.

489
00:40:49,301 --> 00:40:51,053
Why are you acting like this?

490
00:40:51,136 --> 00:40:52,346
What are you mad about?

491
00:40:52,429 --> 00:40:54,014
I told you it's not like that.

492
00:40:55,933 --> 00:40:58,852
Are you keeping your distance from me?

493
00:40:58,936 --> 00:41:00,688
Because I'm your competition or something?

494
00:41:00,771 --> 00:41:02,189
Stop talking nonsense.

495
00:41:02,273 --> 00:41:04,066
What the hell is it then?

496
00:41:04,984 --> 00:41:07,987
One minute you're nice, then you're mad.
Make up your mind, damn it.

497
00:41:08,779 --> 00:41:10,906
Don't piss me off like that.

498
00:41:10,990 --> 00:41:12,992
If you're mad about something,
use your words!

499
00:41:16,453 --> 00:41:20,583
All you have to do is mind your business
and stop being so damn needy!

500
00:41:23,586 --> 00:41:25,212
I already told you.

501
00:41:25,296 --> 00:41:27,006
I didn't play a duet with you
because I wanted to.

502
00:41:27,881 --> 00:41:30,050
I did it to become Mr. Do's student.

503
00:41:30,884 --> 00:41:32,177
I accomplished my goal,

504
00:41:33,012 --> 00:41:35,264
so I don't want to
waste my energy on you.

505
00:41:36,056 --> 00:41:39,059
That's why I want to call it done,
so why the hell do you keep asking?

506
00:41:42,229 --> 00:41:43,981
So that's how you'll talk to me?

507
00:41:45,649 --> 00:41:46,483
All right.

508
00:41:47,443 --> 00:41:48,527
Fine.

509
00:41:49,278 --> 00:41:50,446
It's my fault.

510
00:41:51,572 --> 00:41:53,782
I acted like a clueless, needy loser.

511
00:41:54,783 --> 00:41:56,493
Man, I had no idea.

512
00:41:58,203 --> 00:41:59,997
I got all excited,
thinking we were friends.

513
00:42:15,387 --> 00:42:18,265
Confucianism views humans
not as beings who follow their desires

514
00:42:18,349 --> 00:42:22,061
but as individuals
who must strive for moral perfection.

515
00:42:22,645 --> 00:42:25,189
That's why its core concept
is benevolence,

516
00:42:26,106 --> 00:42:28,400
which is the mindset of caring for others.

517
00:42:28,484 --> 00:42:29,652
Practicing that mindset daily…

518
00:43:24,581 --> 00:43:25,416
Choi Jeong-yo.

519
00:43:26,417 --> 00:43:27,251
Wake up.

520
00:43:28,335 --> 00:43:29,878
You plan to sleep through class?

521
00:43:29,962 --> 00:43:32,464
-Hey, Jeong-yo.
-Hey, wake up.

522
00:43:32,548 --> 00:43:34,049
All right, back to class.

523
00:43:34,133 --> 00:43:34,967
Wake up already.

524
00:43:36,176 --> 00:43:37,344
Where's your textbook?

525
00:43:39,138 --> 00:43:40,097
You don't have it?

526
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:42,808
You punk.
You're in class without your book?

527
00:43:44,017 --> 00:43:45,394
Do you come to school to sleep?

528
00:43:46,311 --> 00:43:48,272
Please leave me alone.

529
00:43:49,106 --> 00:43:50,524
What did you say?

530
00:43:51,108 --> 00:43:53,318
I said just leave me alone.

531
00:43:54,361 --> 00:43:55,279
Choi Jeong-yo.

532
00:43:59,742 --> 00:44:00,743
Come to the teachers' office.

533
00:44:01,744 --> 00:44:02,745
Class is over.

534
00:44:14,882 --> 00:44:15,883
Hey, boys.

535
00:44:15,966 --> 00:44:18,761
The seniors need to practice soccer,
so they want us outside next period.

536
00:44:18,844 --> 00:44:19,887
Come out, okay?

537
00:44:27,561 --> 00:44:28,520
Center it!

538
00:44:28,604 --> 00:44:29,772
Hey, no hitting!

539
00:44:42,367 --> 00:44:43,535
What's your problem?

540
00:44:44,119 --> 00:44:45,788
-What the hell do you want?
-What's going on?

541
00:44:47,122 --> 00:44:48,624
Hey, over here!

542
00:44:50,334 --> 00:44:51,919
-What's happening?
-Hey, wait a minute.

543
00:44:52,002 --> 00:44:54,630
-What's going on?
-Break them up!

544
00:44:54,713 --> 00:44:56,381
Stop them! Hey!

545
00:44:56,465 --> 00:44:57,382
Hey!

546
00:44:57,466 --> 00:44:58,550
Get off me!

547
00:44:58,634 --> 00:45:00,052
You little bastards.

548
00:45:01,595 --> 00:45:04,097
You want me to put you guys in line?

549
00:45:48,976 --> 00:45:51,520
What happened to your face?
Did you get in a fight?

550
00:45:53,564 --> 00:45:54,815
Who did this to you?

551
00:45:56,441 --> 00:45:57,651
You don't need to know.

552
00:45:57,734 --> 00:46:00,237
Of course I need to know.
Just look at your face.

553
00:46:00,320 --> 00:46:01,822
Don't you know looks matter for pianists?

554
00:46:01,905 --> 00:46:03,156
Tell me who did this to you.

555
00:46:04,074 --> 00:46:05,158
Tell me right now!

556
00:46:08,495 --> 00:46:09,872
Just stop it!

557
00:46:11,456 --> 00:46:13,667
Do you need to
keep tabs on everything I do?

558
00:46:14,376 --> 00:46:16,378
I can still play the piano
with a beat-up face!

559
00:46:17,212 --> 00:46:20,090
You're smothering me,
so don't pick me up anymore.

560
00:46:20,757 --> 00:46:25,012
I'm so sick and tired
of you acting like this, Mom!

561
00:46:26,430 --> 00:46:27,389
What's gotten into you?

562
00:46:28,891 --> 00:46:30,309
How dare you take it out on me?

563
00:46:31,393 --> 00:46:33,395
Who do you think I'm doing this for?

564
00:46:35,522 --> 00:46:36,481
You're right.

565
00:46:37,065 --> 00:46:38,775
Because you're doing this for me

566
00:46:38,859 --> 00:46:40,569
and because I know how you feel inside,

567
00:46:40,652 --> 00:46:44,031
I practiced the piano hard
to make you happy.

568
00:46:44,656 --> 00:46:47,618
I worked my fingers to the bone
to make you smile!

569
00:46:49,453 --> 00:46:50,621
But what's the point?

570
00:46:52,998 --> 00:46:53,832
I'm…

571
00:46:55,167 --> 00:46:56,793
not happy at all.

572
00:46:58,754 --> 00:47:02,341
You'll never be happy
unless I'm the best in the world.

573
00:47:03,091 --> 00:47:04,718
So how could I possibly make you happy?

574
00:47:04,801 --> 00:47:06,011
How?

575
00:47:09,473 --> 00:47:10,933
Stop whining.

576
00:47:12,601 --> 00:47:14,102
The competition is just around the corner.

577
00:47:15,646 --> 00:47:16,647
You need to focus.

578
00:47:19,274 --> 00:47:20,275
Mom.

579
00:47:24,112 --> 00:47:25,822
I'm falling apart right now…

580
00:47:27,950 --> 00:47:29,826
and all you care about
is some competition?

581
00:47:42,339 --> 00:47:43,298
Pi-o.

582
00:47:47,427 --> 00:47:48,470
Kang Pi-o!

583
00:48:00,315 --> 00:48:01,566
How about this piece?

584
00:48:02,275 --> 00:48:05,779
Let's say you enter
the upcoming Harmonie Competition.

585
00:48:05,862 --> 00:48:08,115
Besides the required piece,
the piano concerto…

586
00:48:09,282 --> 00:48:10,117
Pi-o?

587
00:48:11,201 --> 00:48:12,035
Hey, Pi-o.

588
00:48:15,414 --> 00:48:16,248
Yes?

589
00:48:16,832 --> 00:48:18,375
Why are you so out of it these days?

590
00:48:20,627 --> 00:48:22,796
You think you can prepare
for the competition like this?

591
00:48:25,799 --> 00:48:27,050
I'm sorry.

592
00:48:48,405 --> 00:48:49,322
Jeong-yo!

593
00:48:50,866 --> 00:48:53,869
Man, it's been a while.

594
00:48:54,619 --> 00:48:56,747
Come over here for a second.

595
00:48:57,372 --> 00:48:58,457
Your dad ran off, didn't he?

596
00:49:06,298 --> 00:49:07,466
I thought we were close.

597
00:49:08,508 --> 00:49:10,635
Why is it so hard to track you down?

598
00:49:13,346 --> 00:49:16,391
I took him in, fed him,
and cut him slack out of pity.

599
00:49:17,893 --> 00:49:20,187
And this is how he repays me?

600
00:49:21,021 --> 00:49:22,355
Where's your dad?

601
00:49:22,439 --> 00:49:24,232
I really don't know.

602
00:49:27,527 --> 00:49:28,487
Stand up straight.

603
00:49:32,199 --> 00:49:34,659
Life is pretty great for you
these days, isn't it?

604
00:49:35,660 --> 00:49:36,578
Grab him.

605
00:49:36,661 --> 00:49:37,829
What?

606
00:49:38,497 --> 00:49:39,331
I said grab him.

607
00:49:40,916 --> 00:49:42,084
Damn it.

608
00:49:42,167 --> 00:49:43,043
Get up.

609
00:49:49,132 --> 00:49:50,050
What was that?

610
00:49:50,842 --> 00:49:51,802
Go take a look.

611
00:50:08,902 --> 00:50:10,278
Hey! You…

612
00:50:45,939 --> 00:50:46,773
Hey, Jeong-yo.

613
00:50:47,482 --> 00:50:50,944
Kim only came here
because other guys have seen you around.

614
00:50:51,027 --> 00:50:52,904
He doesn't know which school you go to.

615
00:50:53,864 --> 00:50:56,074
So just lay low

616
00:50:56,158 --> 00:50:57,909
and don't show up here again.

617
00:50:57,993 --> 00:50:58,910
Got it?

618
00:51:01,913 --> 00:51:02,747
Damn it.

619
00:51:12,340 --> 00:51:14,134
Hey, are you insane?

620
00:51:14,217 --> 00:51:15,844
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

621
00:51:19,347 --> 00:51:20,515
You idiot.

622
00:51:20,599 --> 00:51:22,767
What were you thinking,
getting involved like that?

623
00:51:24,644 --> 00:51:26,605
I couldn't stand by
and let them drag you away.

624
00:51:27,564 --> 00:51:29,482
Stop getting into trouble, will you?

625
00:51:34,112 --> 00:51:35,447
Damn it.

626
00:51:39,951 --> 00:51:41,453
Damn it!

627
00:51:47,125 --> 00:51:49,169
Why were those guys after you?

628
00:51:50,170 --> 00:51:51,213
Isn't it obvious?

629
00:51:51,963 --> 00:51:54,466
If the guy who owes you skips town,
you go after his kid.

630
00:51:56,301 --> 00:51:57,510
And you have no idea

631
00:51:58,929 --> 00:52:00,013
where your father is?

632
00:52:01,431 --> 00:52:03,099
How much debt are we talking about?

633
00:52:05,143 --> 00:52:05,977
Why?

634
00:52:06,686 --> 00:52:07,938
Are you going to pay it off?

635
00:52:08,021 --> 00:52:09,731
What if they show up again?

636
00:52:10,398 --> 00:52:12,275
You need to come up with a plan.

637
00:52:13,026 --> 00:52:16,571
Coming up with a plan
is useless for someone like me.

638
00:52:18,949 --> 00:52:20,075
Forget it.

639
00:52:21,868 --> 00:52:23,328
So why were you a jerk to me?

640
00:52:24,663 --> 00:52:25,497
Tell me.

641
00:52:27,040 --> 00:52:28,166
Why did you treat me like that?

642
00:52:33,838 --> 00:52:34,673
I'm sorry.

643
00:52:35,465 --> 00:52:36,424
It was childish of me.

644
00:52:40,220 --> 00:52:41,096
What?

645
00:52:42,639 --> 00:52:44,015
I mean…

646
00:52:50,689 --> 00:52:51,731
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
TRADITIONAL MARKET

647
00:52:55,318 --> 00:52:56,278
If you're sorry,

648
00:52:57,195 --> 00:52:58,321
come with me somewhere.

649
00:52:59,781 --> 00:53:00,615
Where?

650
00:53:01,199 --> 00:53:02,701
Will you come or not?

651
00:53:29,269 --> 00:53:33,565
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

652
00:53:45,869 --> 00:53:46,703
Come in.

653
00:53:56,671 --> 00:53:57,547
What's this?

654
00:53:58,298 --> 00:53:59,549
I never knew this place was here.

655
00:54:00,425 --> 00:54:02,969
It used to be a warehouse
where pianos were brought in for repairs.

656
00:54:03,678 --> 00:54:05,305
I've been coming here since I was a kid.

657
00:54:14,773 --> 00:54:17,734
No one would buy that
because it's too old.

658
00:54:17,817 --> 00:54:18,651
CHOI JEONG-YO

659
00:54:18,735 --> 00:54:19,944
Which works out great for me.

660
00:54:26,618 --> 00:54:27,702
This is what we're here for.

661
00:54:40,131 --> 00:54:41,591
You played all of these?

662
00:54:42,342 --> 00:54:43,176
Yeah.

663
00:54:44,677 --> 00:54:46,429
After my mom passed away…

664
00:54:48,431 --> 00:54:50,058
I hated playing the piano.

665
00:54:51,226 --> 00:54:53,103
But for some reason,
playing made me happy.

666
00:54:55,105 --> 00:54:57,107
That's why I spent a lot of time here.

667
00:55:05,949 --> 00:55:07,283
This one doesn't have any notes.

668
00:55:11,788 --> 00:55:12,747
It's a four-hands piece.

669
00:55:14,124 --> 00:55:17,335
I heard it somewhere
and said it was really good,

670
00:55:17,419 --> 00:55:19,003
so my mom got it for me.

671
00:55:22,590 --> 00:55:23,758
But we never got to play it.

672
00:55:25,552 --> 00:55:28,388
Did your mom play the piano well?

673
00:55:30,223 --> 00:55:31,099
Yeah.

674
00:55:33,143 --> 00:55:35,603
She was actually my piano teacher.

675
00:55:41,985 --> 00:55:44,028
Then let's play this before we go.

676
00:55:45,321 --> 00:55:46,197
Right now?

677
00:55:46,865 --> 00:55:47,699
Yeah.

678
00:55:50,994 --> 00:55:54,038
This time, you play the secondo,
and I'll play the primo.

679
00:55:54,122 --> 00:55:56,916
You handle the pedal,
and I'll turn the pages.

680
00:55:57,000 --> 00:55:57,959
Okay.

681
00:56:00,712 --> 00:56:01,921
Hold on to this memory.

682
00:56:02,839 --> 00:56:03,923
Remember this practice room

683
00:56:04,966 --> 00:56:05,925
and…

684
00:56:07,969 --> 00:56:09,053
today's performance.

685
00:58:02,208 --> 00:58:03,167
Hey, Jeong-yo.

686
00:58:06,296 --> 00:58:07,839
Let's be practice partners.

687
00:58:10,425 --> 00:58:11,426
What do you mean?

688
00:58:12,969 --> 00:58:15,263
You said you were too busy
preparing for the competition.

689
00:58:16,764 --> 00:58:18,224
No, I'm not entering.

690
00:58:18,891 --> 00:58:20,727
I want to be your practice partner

691
00:58:20,810 --> 00:58:23,938
and find a way to be happy making music.

692
00:58:24,689 --> 00:58:26,149
You'll help me, right?

693
00:58:43,333 --> 00:58:44,167
No.

694
00:58:48,838 --> 00:58:50,048
Kang Pi-o!

695
00:58:52,634 --> 00:58:54,177
Hey, stop!

696
00:58:54,844 --> 00:58:56,846
Let go of me! Let go!

697
00:58:58,056 --> 00:58:58,931
Enough!

698
00:59:05,480 --> 00:59:06,481
Are you insane?

699
00:59:07,065 --> 00:59:08,733
This is all your fault.

700
00:59:10,360 --> 00:59:12,362
It's all your fault!

701
00:59:37,470 --> 00:59:39,597
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

702
00:59:40,181 --> 00:59:41,974
I've decided not to enter the competition.

703
00:59:42,475 --> 00:59:45,687
I don't think I've ever played the piano
because it was fun.

704
00:59:46,688 --> 00:59:47,897
Fine, then quit!

705
00:59:47,980 --> 00:59:49,941
To hell with lessons and school!

706
00:59:50,983 --> 00:59:52,276
His family must be rich.

707
00:59:52,860 --> 00:59:54,028
Give me his number.

708
00:59:54,112 --> 00:59:56,322
Sir, he has nothing to do with this.

709
00:59:56,906 --> 00:59:58,366
So? What do we do now?

710
00:59:59,075 --> 01:00:00,785
Are you uncomfortable around me?

711
01:00:00,868 --> 01:00:02,787
-Where are you?
-You curious?

712
01:00:04,747 --> 01:00:05,581
Kang Pi-o!

713
01:00:08,126 --> 01:00:13,131
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

